WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.506
Week 13: City, Directions, and Public Services. ask for and give directions identify public services confirm a route

2
00:00:08.506 --> 00:00:21.580
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can ask for and give directions, identify public services, confirm a route. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:29.211
Language system. Ir a; location prepositions; informal commands for directions; seguir and doblar.

4
00:00:29.211 --> 00:00:36.587
Sound and delivery. Distinguish but accept seseo and distinción; practice place names respectfully.

5
00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:46.119
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:46.119 --> 00:01:11.887
Model language. Siga derecho hasta la plaza. — Go straight to the plaza. Doble a la izquierda en la segunda esquina. — Turn left at the second corner. ¿Voy bien para el ayuntamiento? — Am I going the right way to city hall? Nos perdimos cerca de la estación. — We got lost near the station. El banco queda enfrente del correo. — The bank is across from the post office.

7
00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:21.891
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
